Z||000000||hugh||12-21-2000||08:29 PM||||This past year my brother and I have spent a ton of money fixing up our shop.We turned it into a nice place that could support a couple of business's when it gets to be time to retire(hah)On Satirday we finished blowing the insulation into the ceiling.On Sunday the winds we had lifted the rubber roofing off,pulling out the nails as it did.When I went to the shop on Sunday morning it was raining harder inside than it was outside(not exagerating).All our new insulation,plasterboard,new parts,tools were wet.The insurance adjuster was here on Wednesday to check it out.We will probably not lose too much,but the agravation of going from a nice,clean,new,fresh,shop to a mess is sure depressing.I was hoping letting this out would help me feel better about it,but I don't think it will.Thanks for listening.||||reg||1
